      "solution": "import sys\n\nn = int(input())\nvals = list(map(int, input().split()))\neven = sum(x for x in vals if x % 2 == 0)\nodd = sum(x for x in vals if x % 2)\nprint(even - odd)",
      "statement": "You are auditing a warehouse inventory log. Each line item has a quantity. For reporting, you need the balance between even and odd quantities: the sum of all even values minus the sum of all odd values.\n\n**Goal**\n\nGiven `n` integers, output `(sum of even numbers) - (sum of odd numbers)`.\n\n**Example**\n\nFor `1 2 3 4`, evens are `2 + 4 = 6`, odds are `1 + 3 = 4`, so the answer is `6 - 4 = 2`.",
